Actually, using SELECT new ... (known as a Constructor Expression in JPQL) is a valid and very efficient way to fetch data. However, in your specific case, there are two reasons why it feels "wrong" or "messy":
 * Hardcoding the Package Path: It makes the query very long and fragile. If you move your DTO to a different package, the query will break, and the IDE might not always catch it.
 * Coupling: It tightly couples your database logic to a specific UI/Transfer object.
Is it actually "Wrong"?
Technically: No. It is high-performance because Hibernate selects only the columns needed for the DTO rather than the entire Entity.
Architecturally: Yes, it's a bit "smelly."
The Better Way: Using Projections (Interfaces)
The "Spring Data JPA" way to do this without writing long package names is to use an Interface-based Projection.
Step 1: Create a Projection Interface
Instead of a Class (DTO), create an interface. Spring will automatically create the implementation for you.
package com.fincore.YearEndService.Repository.Projection;

import java.math.BigDecimal;
import java.time.LocalDate;

public interface IProfitLossSummary {
    LocalDate getTransferDate();
    Integer getCircleBranchCode();
    BigDecimal getTotalProfitLoss();
}

Step 2: Simplify the Query
Now your repository doesn't need the full package name. You just alias the columns to match the "get" methods in the interface.
@Query("SELECT p.transferDate as transferDate, " +
       "p.circleBranchCode as circleBranchCode, " +
       "SUM(p.profitLoss) as totalProfitLoss " +
       "FROM ProfitLossTransfer p " +
       "GROUP BY p.circleBranchCode, p.transferDate " +
       "ORDER BY p.transferDate DESC")
List<IProfitLossSummary> findProfitLossSummaryGroupedByCircle();

Why this is better:
 * Cleaner Code: No long strings like new com.fincore.YearEndService.DTO....
 * Refactor Friendly: If you rename your DTO or move packages, the Repository doesn't care.
 * Readability: The query looks like standard SQL/JPQL.
What about your Service?
In your ProfitLossServiceImpl, you can still return your ProfitLossSummaryDto by mapping the interface results:
@Override
public List<ProfitLossSummaryDto> getCircleWiseSummary() {
    return repository.findProfitLossSummaryGroupedByCircle().stream()
        .map(p -> new ProfitLossSummaryDto(
            p.getTransferDate(), 
            p.getCircleBranchCode(), 
            p.getTotalProfitLoss()
        ))
        .collect(Collectors.toList());
}

Recommendation
If you are working in a Senior/Tech Lead capacity as we discussed, Projections are considered the cleaner, more professional standard.
